  "additional_concerns": [
    "The home-supervision statement establishes the measures' purpose, not expressly an independent item (ii) eligibility condition. Item (i) expressly requires supervision; importing that condition into item (ii) is unsupported. A broader contextual interpretation remains unresolved.",
    "Nodes node.1bf6918f69c6b37738daeb83, node.4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e, node.ce439b1cf9ed8301fbb68f94 and node.ea4d19630f8cab09065b1909 convert preserved application processing into an exclusion from relief. Continued processing is explicit; substantive disqualification and its duration are not. These formulas implement proposed interpretations rather than an established complete transition rule.",
    "Node node.4d548f2e09bc36ef51212f64 excludes legacy applications from scope and consequently leaves their treatment unanswered. Node node.b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffa tests substantive conditions alone and cannot establish actual procedural relief.",
    "Node node.8eb374ffa546ddd2ba291e37 supplies no executable formalization. Its unresolved actual-relief question must not produce a known Boolean merely from substantive qualification or preserved processing.",
    "The specific 28 November 2025 commencement provision supports the selected date, but must be read alongside the introductory immediate-effect wording. Neither provision establishes a universal implementation-date test or resolves every subsequent application-history event.",
    "The updated UCITS FAQs and existing approval or authorisation rules are missing authorities needed to resolve actual procedural availability, transition duration, and any withdrawal or resubmission treatment. Neither opaque supplied dependency ID can reliably be matched to those authorities; neither has a non-null source_hash.",
    "Applicable home-jurisdiction requirements and any authoritative classification guidance for novel or complex features and possible local policy implications are absent. The executable candidates accept these legal judgments as inputs; they do not establish them.",
    "The claim-specific NONE_DECLARED assessments concern support for the two express circular statements only. They do not establish that the candidates' complete relief rules need no external authority."
  ],
